# The backend's SQLite file, its WAL, and anything else written at runtime.
# The schema and the import are code; the database they produce is not.
server/data

# The Base44 export the backend is seeded from. It is NOT reference material
# like `updates/` — it is the old app's live database, and it carries names,
# email addresses, phone numbers, card last-fours, wallet addresses and
# transaction records belonging to identifiable people. It must never reach a
# remote, and `db/import.ts` is the only thing that reads it. A clone without
# it migrates and serves normally; the import reports "nothing (new-data/ not
# found)" and moves on. The two spec PDFs live there too, and go the same way
# for the simpler reason that they are commercial documents.
new-data/

# Local build variables. `.env.local` is already covered by `*.local` above, but
# a plain `.env` was not — and this is the file people actually create.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
